## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

This is a textbook case of **"coverage without verification"** — every production method is exercised but almost nothing is actually asserted. These tests would pass even if every method returned garbage or corrupted data.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Assertion-Free Tests (No Verification At All)

| # | Test | Problem |
|---|------|---------|
| 1 | `AddProduct_Works` (L17-21) | Calls `AddProduct` then stops. Never verifies the product was stored. |
| 2 | `UpdatePrice_Works` (L33-35) | Updates price, never checks the new price took effect. Could silently no-op. |
| 3 | `RemoveProduct_Works` (L38-42) | Removes product, never verifies it's gone. Delete could be broken entirely. |
| 4 | `GetProductCount_Works` (L63-66) | Assigns count to a local variable and discards it. Zero assertions. |
| 5 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L68-74) | Applies 10% discount, never checks any price changed. The core business logic is completely unverified. |
| 6 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L85-88) | Imports data, never checks it's retrievable or correctly parsed. |

**Fix pattern:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);
    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}

[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesStoredPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")?.Price);
}

[TestMethod]
public void ApplyBulkDiscount_ReducesAllPrices()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 100m));
    _catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
    Assert.AreEqual(90m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")?.Price);
}
```

---

### 🟠 HIGH — Shallow/Trivial Assertions

| # | Test | Problem |
|---|------|---------|
| 7 | `GetProduct_Works` (L24-29) | Only asserts `IsNotNull`. Never checks SKU, Name, or Price match what was stored. A method returning `new Product("","",0)` would pass. |
